{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLazyFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function is used for creating a partial file-based route instance that is lazily loaded when matched. This route instance can only be used to configure the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guide/code-splitting.md#how-does-tanstack-router-split-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-critical properties"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the route, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createlazyfileroute-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createLazyFileRoute options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLazyFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a single argument of type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that represents the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" of the file that the route will be generated from."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"path","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required, but "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"automatically inserted and updated by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr generate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr watch"},{"type":"text","value":" commands"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full path of the file that the route will be generated from."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createlazyfileroute-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createLazyFileRoute returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new function that accepts a single argument of partial of the type "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouteOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that will be used to configure the file "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouteType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instance."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"Pick<\n  RouteOptions,\n  'component' | 'pendingComponent' | 'errorComponent' | 'notFoundComponent'\n>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./RouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouteOptions"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ Note: For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr generate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr watch"},{"type":"text","value":" to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"},{"type":"text","value":" identifier."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/')({\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"createlazyfileroute-options","text":"createLazyFileRoute options","level":2},{"id":"path","text":"path","level":3},{"id":"createlazyfileroute-returns","text":"createLazyFileRoute returns","level":3},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `createLazyFileRoute` function is used for creating a partial file-based route instance that is lazily loaded when matched. This route instance can only be used to configure the [non-critical properties](../../guide/code-splitting.md#how-does-tanstack-router-split-code) of the route, such as `component`, `pendingComponent`, `errorComponent`, and the `notFoundComponent`.\n\n## createLazyFileRoute options\n\nThe `createLazyFileRoute` function accepts a single argument of type `string` that represents the `path` of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### `path`\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Required, but **automatically inserted and updated by the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands**\n- The full path of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### createLazyFileRoute returns\n\nA new function that accepts a single argument of partial of the type [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md) that will be used to configure the file [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nPick<\n  RouteOptions,\n  'component' | 'pendingComponent' | 'errorComponent' | 'notFoundComponent'\n>\n```\n\n- [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n\n> ⚠️ Note: For `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the `Route` identifier.\n\n### Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/')({\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createLazyFileRouteFunction\ntitle: createLazyFileRoute function\n---\n\nThe `createLazyFileRoute` function is used for creating a partial file-based route instance that is lazily loaded when matched. This route instance can only be used to configure the [non-critical properties](../../guide/code-splitting.md#how-does-tanstack-router-split-code) of the route, such as `component`, `pendingComponent`, `errorComponent`, and the `notFoundComponent`.\n\n## createLazyFileRoute options\n\nThe `createLazyFileRoute` function accepts a single argument of type `string` that represents the `path` of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### `path`\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Required, but **automatically inserted and updated by the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands**\n- The full path of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### createLazyFileRoute returns\n\nA new function that accepts a single argument of partial of the type [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md) that will be used to configure the file [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nPick<\n  RouteOptions,\n  'component' | 'pendingComponent' | 'errorComponent' | 'notFoundComponent'\n>\n```\n\n- [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n\n> ⚠️ Note: For `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the `Route` identifier.\n\n### Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/')({\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n"}
